THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

app/src/main/assets/models/yolov8m_seg_int8.tflite
    YOLOv8m-seg by Ultralytics, licensed under AGPL-3.0 (https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics).
    Exported with Ultralytics' own TFLite exporter, int8-quantized:
        from ultralytics import YOLO
        YOLO("yolov8m-seg.pt").export(format="tflite", int8=True, data="coco128-seg.yaml")

app/src/main/assets/models/ocr/det.tflite, rec_arabic.tflite, rec_cyrillic.tflite, dict_*.txt
    PP-OCRv5 mobile text detection (PP-OCRv5_mobile_det) and recognition (arabic_ and
    cyrillic_PP-OCRv5_mobile_rec) by PaddlePaddle, licensed under Apache-2.0
    (https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR). Converted from the official ONNX releases
    (huggingface.co/PaddlePaddle/<model>_onnx): ONNX -> PyTorch with onnx2torch -> LiteRT with
    litert-torch, as fixed-size signatures sharing one set of weights (detector 960x960, 960x736,
    736x960, 960x544, 544x960; recognizer 48 high x 320/640/960/1280/1920 wide), then weight-only
    int8 quantized with ai-edge-quantizer (recipe weight_only_wi8_afp32). Outputs were checked
    against ONNX Runtime before quantization. dict_*.txt are the models' character_dict lists from
    their inference.yml.

Google ML Kit (play-services-mlkit-text-recognition*, -barcode-scanning, -image-labeling)
    Proprietary, used under the ML Kit Terms of Service (https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/terms).

The on-device vision-language models (Gemma 4, InternVL3.5, Qwen2-VL) are not part of this repository;
